Native numerical suite and image preprocessing

The image processor resize conventions follow PyTorch's pinned antialiasing
implementation, as recorded in the T07/T08 provenance.

The FP32/BF16 long-row softmax reduction independently implements the accumulation
and alignment conventions of PyTorch 5c4886908584029761b579af026dcfb627c84070:
aten/src/ATen/native/cuda/SoftMax.cu
aten/src/ATen/native/cuda/block_reduce.cuh

The short-row RMS reduction follows the FP32 mean's vector accumulation and
block/warp reduction order in the same revision:
aten/src/ATen/native/cuda/Reduce.cuh

The channel-major FP32 L2 reduction follows the same revision's strided
reduction geometry, four interleaved accumulators and vertical reduction tree:
aten/src/ATen/native/cuda/Reduce.cuh
aten/src/ATen/native/SharedReduceOps.h (NormTwoOps)

The channel-major audio RMS reduction uses the same Reduce.cuh geometry with
separate FP32 square/mean/affine operations before one BF16 output cast.

DS4 modifications: C numeric API, explicit interval masks, in-place output,
resource ownership and native CUDA dispatch. No PyTorch runtime dependency.
